Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:59:32 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Input: stmpe-keypad: add STMPE1801 support

STMPE1801 uses different keypad register addresses and swaps the row and
column fields in FIFO events. Its 8-by-10 matrix also needs a four-bit
row shift, so the old fixed 64-entry keymap is too small.

Describe the register and event layout per variant, allocate the matrix
keymap from the firmware dimensions, validate decoded coordinates before
indexing it, and drain the ten-entry STMPE1801 FIFO. Keep scan disabled
until IRQ and input registration have succeeded, and unwind the block
enable vote on every initialization fault.

On a failed scan-start transaction, make a best-effort stop attempt
before disabling the keypad block and preserve the original start error.
Report stop failures during both probe unwind and remove. Factor the
bounded FIFO drain and scan lifecycle ordering into internal helpers
shared with KUnit only when KUnit is enabled.

